## 6. Repair Strategy — Simplified

Instead of tangent snap + iterative push-out, we use a single **nearest-feasible-location** repair:

```python
def repair_to_feasible(waypoint, prev_wp, next_wp, buildings, max_retries=REPAIR_MAX_RETRIES):
    """Move waypoint to nearest position where both adjacent edges clear all buildings."""
    
    for attempt in range(max_retries):
        if segment_is_feasible(prev_wp, waypoint, buildings) and \
           segment_is_feasible(waypoint, next_wp, buildings):
            return waypoint  # already feasible
        
        # Find the blocking building
        blocker = find_blocking_building(prev_wp, waypoint, next_wp, buildings)
        
        # Move waypoint to the nearest corner of the blocker + clearance offset
        corners = get_corners_with_clearance(blocker, REPAIR_CLEARANCE)
        
        # Pick the corner that minimizes total detour distance
        best_corner = min(corners, key=lambda c: 
            dist(prev_wp, c) + dist(c, next_wp))
        
        # Only accept if this corner has line-of-sight to both neighbors
        if segment_is_feasible(prev_wp, best_corner, buildings) and \
           segment_is_feasible(best_corner, next_wp, buildings):
            return best_corner
        
        waypoint = best_corner  # try again from new position
    
    return None  # repair failed — discard this offspring
```

This is simpler, deterministic, and covers the same intent: route around the blocking obstacle via its nearest visible corner.

